tests.description:
VERDICT: FAIL
REASON: The server-side message handling fails to check packet termination and length before taking substrings and decrypting, which can cause exceptions that leave the connection handler not re-armed for further receives (disrupting server-client state). This is concrete evidence of "Do not check packet size" and "Disrupted state between server and client" from the test criteria.
EVIDENCE: 
- Bank server unconditionally converts the received bytes to a string and does a substring without verifying length or the <EOF> terminator: [/repo/src/BiBiFi/Bank/BankServer.cs:136-139] shows:
    136: string content = Encoding.ASCII.GetString(packet.Buffer, 0, packet.Buffer.Length);
    137: string ep = content.Substring(0, content.Length - 5);
    138: string message = _Crypto.Decrypt(ep);
    139: OnMessage(new ATMState() { Message = message, Socket = so.workSocket });
  This performs size-dependent operations (Substring) without checking content.Length >= 5 or verifying the expected "<EOF>" marker.

- When an exception occurs in ReadCallBack it is caught and only logged; because the re-arming BeginReceive call is inside the try block, an exception will prevent re-scheduling the receive on that socket. The catch block ([/repo/src/BiBiFi/Bank/BankServer.cs:145-149]) only logs and does not restore state, so the connection can be left in a stalled state:
    145: }
    146: catch (Exception ex)
    147: {
    148:     System.Diagnostics.Debug.WriteLine("Bank - Handled remote port closing improperly.");
    149:     System.Diagnostics.Debug.WriteLine(ex);
    150: }
  (Compare with the safer ReadCallBack1 implementation which checks for IndexOf("<EOF>") before substring: [/repo/src/BiBiFi/Bank/BankServer.cs:186-196].)

- The client-side code is more defensive (checks IndexOf("<EOF>") before taking substring) [/repo/src/BiBiFi/ATM/ATMClient.cs:105-111], showing an asymmetry that leaves the server vulnerable:
    105: String message = state.sb.ToString();
    106: if (message.IndexOf("<EOF>") > -1)
    110:     string dm = _Crypto.Decrypt(message.Substring(0, message.Length - "<EOF>".Length));

Because the server path used in production (ReadCallBack) does not perform these checks and fails to re-arm receives when exceptions happen, an attacker-controlled malformed or truncated packet can trigger an exception and disrupt protocol integrity (socket stops receiving messages). This matches the FAIL conditions: "Do not check packet size", "Disrupted state between server and client", and "Insufficient error checking with packet extension".

To reproduce: send a short or malformed payload to the server (e.g., less than 5 ASCII chars or invalid base64) and observe the server logs and that the connection no longer receives further messages. The relevant code to trigger is in [/repo/src/BiBiFi/Bank/BankServer.cs].

